== 1. the framework owns a component's signals ==
ok   it rendered: <p>0</p>
ok   nothing was refused — the signal was NOT deaf: 
ok   and the framework owned it: true
ok   a write moved the page with no on_init anywhere: <p>3</p>

== 2. THE CONTROL: a signal reflection cannot see ==
ok   it renders: <p>0</p>
ok   and it IS deaf, loudly: 0: live expression 1 read no signal
ok   so a write moves nothing: <p>0</p>

== 3. a view-model is attached, and its signals owned ==
ok   the model was attached exactly once: 1
ok   it knows its component: true
ok   the page rendered: <p>0</p>
ok   nothing was refused: 

== 4. a command runs, and its guard is asked twice ==
ok   the command can run: true
ok   running it moved the page through the model's signal: <p>1</p>
ok   the command now refuses: false
ok   and running it anyway does nothing: <p>1</p>

== 5. a command with no owner is inert ==
ok   it cannot run: false
ok   and running it did not fail

== 6. a page UNDER A LAYOUT is wired the same way ==
ok   the page rendered inside its layout: <div><p>0</p></div>
ok   nothing was refused: 
ok   its signal was owned: true
ok   its view-model was attached: 1
ok   and its @inject field was filled — not left at its default: tick2
ok   so a signal write moves the page through the layout: <div><p>4</p></div>
